      "text": "The volume of the pyramid will remain the same relative to the base when it is cut. Therefore, the volume of the smaller pyramid will be one-fourth the volume of the original pyramid.\n\n$\\text{Volume of frustum } = \\text{Volume of original pyramid} - \\text{Volume of smaller pyramid}$\n\n$\\text{Volume of smaller pyramid } = \\frac{1}{4} \\times \\text{Volume of original pyramid }$\n\n$\\text{Volume of frustum } = \\left(\\frac{1}{4} \\text{ of original pyramid}\\right) - \\left(\\frac{1}{4} \\text{ of original pyramid}\\right)$\nTo solve for the volume of the frustum, we first need to determine the volume of the original pyramid and the smaller pyramid. Let's denote the volume of the original pyramid as \\( V_{\\text{original}} \\) and the volume of the smaller pyramid as \\( V_{\\text{small}} \\).\n\nThe formula for the volume of a pyramid is given by:\n\n\\[ V = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{Base Area} \\times \\text{Height} \\]\n\nFirst, let's calculate the volume of the original pyramid:\n\n\\[ V_{\\text{original}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 12^2 \\times 8 \\]\n\nNow, let's calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid:\n\n\\[ V_{\\text{small}} = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 6^2 \\times 4 \\]\n\nFinally, we can find the volume of the frustum by subtracting the volume of the smaller pyramid from the volume of the original pyramid:\n\n\\[ V_{\\text{frustum}} = V_{\\text{original}} - V_{\\text{small}} \\]\n\nLet's calculate these volumes step-by-step using Python.\n```python\n# Define the dimensions of the original and smaller pyramids\nbase_edge_original = 12\nheight_original = 8\nbase_edge_small = 6\nheight_small = 4\n\n# Calculate the volume of the original pyramid\nvolume_original = (1/3) * base_edge_original**2 * height_original\n\n# Calculate the volume of the smaller pyramid\nvolume_small = (1/3) * base_edge_small**2 * height_small\n\n# Calculate the volume of the frustum\nvolume_frustum = volume_original - volume_small\nprint(volume_frustum)\n```\n```output\n192.0\n```\nThe volume of the frustum is \\(\\boxed{192}\\) cubic centimeters.",
